Ankûre jî bigir, ho ankûre heşîn e, heşîn e haye, welle bîra
avê li vir haye.
 
Film the grapes too, look the grapes are green, green they
are, by God there is a water well here.

739
00:44:26,000 --> 00:44:30,000
Ehê!
 
Aha!

740
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:36,000
Bîra avê li vir haye.
 
There is a water well here.

741
00:44:36,000 --> 00:44:41,000
Arê, Ebû Mhemed, şabab li Efrîn bîn, noka ew jî Efrîn tên
wavo?
 
Yes, Abu Muhammad, the guys were in Afrin, now they are
coming from Afrin like that?

742
00:44:41,000 --> 00:44:45,000
Oo, o vwa noka jî Efrîn tên. Lûr biiskinîn, lûr biiskinîn,
were.
 
Oh, look right now they are coming from Afrin. Stop right
here, stop right here, come.

743
00:44:45,000 --> 00:44:49,000
Aa, oo yat, xolû yat.
 
Ah, look he came, the uncle came.

744
00:44:49,000 --> 00:44:51,000
O me dîtî.
 
We saw him.

745
00:44:51,000 --> 00:44:53,000
Ebû Mhemed, lê serke, nebî lê serke.
 
Abu Muhammad, look at him, look at the prophet [look
closely].

746
00:44:53,000 --> 00:44:55,000
Oo, dilê ma bavra dogrî ye.
 
Oh, our hearts are true to each other.

747
00:44:55,000 --> 00:44:56,000
De were.
 
Come on then.

748
00:44:56,000 --> 00:44:58,000
Miştaro deng şewitî o, miştaro deng şewitî.
 
The "Mixtar" (village head) lost his voice, the Mixtar lost
his voice.

749
00:44:58,000 --> 00:44:59,000
Arê.
 
Yes.

750
00:44:59,000 --> 00:45:03,000
Arê Ebû Mhemed, tabeen em îro li vî derê ne, cem Ebû Salah.
 
Yes Abu Muhammad, naturally we are here today, with Abu
Salah.

751
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:05,000
Silavê meşter hene, ortê hewşê da.
 
Many greetings, in the middle of the courtyard.

752
00:45:05,000 --> 00:45:11,000
Tabeen, ma hat gund sawirand, em ser xênî bûn, me dî Ebû
Salah ji Efrîn tê.
 
Naturally, we came and filmed the village, we were on the
roof, we saw Abu Salah coming from Afrin.

753
00:45:11,000 --> 00:45:12,000
Ebû Salah, keremke.
 
Abu Salah, welcome.

754
00:45:12,000 --> 00:45:13,000
Mago merheba ştaro.
 
I said hello to you.

755
00:45:13,000 --> 00:45:14,000
Meya ehlen we sehlen.
 
A hundred welcomes.

756
00:45:14,000 --> 00:45:20,000
Me hat nav gundê we teswîr kir, tabeen xwestekê Ebû Mhemed û
xwestekê milletê gundî we ye.
 
We came and filmed your village, naturally it was the
request of Abu Muhammad and the request of the people of
your village.

757
00:45:20,000 --> 00:45:24,000
Te çi silavê dişîne ji Ebû Mhemed ra li ta ser dike, liko
mubaşer. Silav kê bişîne, hey pigirê.
 
What greetings do you send to Abu Muhammad who is watching
you, right here directly. Send a greeting, here hold this.

758
00:45:24,000 --> 00:45:30,000
Xalê min e, we êmez cwar dikim, we jêra silavê min jêra
hene, heta bi Elmanya jêra.
 
He is my uncle [brother-in-law], and I respect him, and to
him I have greetings, all the way to Germany for him.

759
00:45:30,000 --> 00:45:31,000
Maşalla, maşalla.
 
Mashallah, mashallah.

760
00:45:31,000 --> 00:45:33,000
Silavê meşter hene heta çi Elmanya?
 
Many greetings all the way to what, Germany?

761
00:45:33,000 --> 00:45:35,000
Arê, ser serê min, ser çavê min.
 
Yes, on my head, on my eyes.

762
00:45:35,000 --> 00:45:36,000
Çavê te sax bin.
 
May your eyes be healthy.

763
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:42,000
Xolû, navê gundî we me jê xolêkî pirs kir, dibê min go xê
nav lêkirin Çomaznê?
 
Uncle, regarding your village name, I asked an uncle, he
said... I said why did they name it Çomaznê?

764
00:45:42,000 --> 00:45:48,000
Dibê berê gic dar hebû, û çoyê xwe jî gic qaling bûn, ê
zingê xwe dibê lêkirin...
 
It says there used to be tough trees, and their sticks were
very thick, and they named their zinc/rust...

765
00:45:48,000 --> 00:45:49,000
Ecem... berê gic ço bû.
 
Strange... before it was very much "stick" [wood].

766
00:45:49,000 --> 00:45:50,000
Eywa.
 
Yes.

767
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:55,000
No ko ço bû, nav lê nan Çomazn bû, nav lê nan Çomazn.
 
Since it was "stick" [wood], they named it Çomazn, they
named it Çomazn.

768
00:45:55,000 --> 00:45:56,000
Ne Çomaznê?
 
Not Çomaznê?

769
00:45:56,000 --> 00:45:57,000
Çomazn.
 
Çomazn.

770
00:45:57,000 --> 00:45:59,000
Ço-Mezin.
 
Big-Stick.

771
00:45:59,000 --> 00:46:01,000
Eywa, berê ço bû, Çomazn bû.
 
Yes, before it was "stick", so it was Çomazn [Big Stick].

772
00:46:01,000 --> 00:46:03,000
Dibê Çomazno.
 
They say Çomazno.

773
00:46:03,000 --> 00:46:03,000
Çoyê mezin.
 
Yes.

774
00:46:03,000 --> 00:46:05,000
Çoyê mezin.
 
Big stick.

775
00:46:05,000 --> 00:46:07,000
Lê berê ço bû.
 
But before it was "stick" [wooded].

776
00:46:07,000 --> 00:46:08,000
Eywa.
 
Yes.

777
00:46:08,000 --> 00:46:11,000
Xolû, gundî we bi çi meşûr e?
 
Uncle, what is your village famous for?

778
00:46:11,000 --> 00:46:12,000
Gundî me bi her tişkî meşûr e.
 
Our village is famous for everything.

779
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:18,000
Kîjan aîla têda, tê naskirin? Aîla mesela kîjan malbata esas
hatî vî darê?
 
Which families are known in it? For example, which original
family came to this place?

780
00:46:18,000 --> 00:46:21,000
Bi Xwedê gund esas yek e.
 
By God, the village is basically one.

781
00:46:21,000 --> 00:46:23,000
Kîjan, bi kîjan aîlê tê naskirin?
 
Which... by which family is it known?

782
00:46:23,000 --> 00:46:26,000
Bi Mala Nasê tê naskirin û bi Mala Şêxû tê naskirin.
 
It is known by the Nasê Family and known by the Sheikho
Family.

783
00:46:26,000 --> 00:46:28,000
Mala Nasê û Mala Şêxû.
 
Nasê Family and Sheikho Family.

784
00:46:28,000 --> 00:46:33,000
Maşalla, maşalla. Gundekî we gellek cûcûk e, bes maşalla
xweş e, kîbar e.
 
Mashallah, mashallah. Your village is very small, but
mashallah it is nice, it is elegant.

785
00:46:33,000 --> 00:46:35,000
Bes rêkê we gic qorçox in ne.
 
But your roads are very bumpy/steep, aren't they.

786
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:39,000
Bi Xwedê, el-esas em rêkê çêkin yanî, esas em hew dikin.
 
By God, basically we are fixing the roads, basically we are
trying.

787
00:46:39,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Megû vê gundo zilimîyî di vî darê da. E giya zivt e, bes şar
heye qorçox in, bes ê we ji ewelî da qorçox e heta vir.
 
I said this village is oppressed in this place. It's all
asphalt [elsewhere], but there is a city that is bumpy, but
yours is bumpy from the beginning up to here.

788
00:46:46,000 --> 00:46:47,000
Arê. Arê.
 
Yes. Yes.

789
00:46:47,000 --> 00:46:49,000
Xwestek ne ta din hene wulo xolû?
 
Do you have any other requests like that uncle?

790
00:46:49,000 --> 00:46:52,000
No welle saeta we xweş, û Xwedê ji we razî be.
 
No by God, may your time be happy, and may God be pleased
with you.

791
00:46:52,000 --> 00:46:53,000
Ser serê min, ser çavê min.
 
On my head, on my eyes.

792
00:46:53,000 --> 00:46:55,000
Serî te sax bin.
 
May your head be healthy [Long life to you].

793
00:46:55,000 --> 00:46:59,000
Arê, hevalno, li vî derê jî em vîdya xwe xîtam dikin.
 
Yes, friends, here we also end our video.

794
00:46:59,000 --> 00:47:03,000
Tabeen me gund wara sawirand, û me gundî berko jî sawirand.
 
Naturally, we filmed the village for you, and we filmed the
village of Berko/nearby too.

795
00:47:03,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Me gû di vîdya xwe da ekserî vîdî me gic efewî ne.
 
I said in our video, mostly our videos are very spontaneous.

796
00:47:06,000 --> 00:47:10,000
Silavê me ji wera hene. Cûcûk, mezin, çavê giya maç dikim.
 
Our greetings to you. Small, big, I kiss everyone's eyes.

797
00:47:10,000 --> 00:47:15,000
Çi kol dibe, çi pîr dibe, çi kaş dibe, çi xûr dibe. Silavê
me ji giya ra hene.
 
Whether young, whether old, whether uphill, whether
downhill. Our greetings to everyone.

798
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:19,000
Bi mera bin dîsa vîdyekî din xweş, kîbar, inşalla emê wara
daxin nîzik da.
 
Stay with us for another nice, elegant video, God willing we
will upload it for you soon.

799
00:47:19,000 --> 00:47:22,000
Teelîqê we pirr bin, inşalla vîdî me be ecibînin.
 
May your comments be many, God willing you will like our
videos.

800
00:47:22,000 --> 00:47:24,000
Xatirê we, gula gula, bay bay ke xolû.
 
Goodbye, with flowers [farewell], wave bye-bye uncle.

801
00:47:24,000 --> 00:47:26,000
Bay bay. Ebû Mhemed, silav, silav, silav.
 
Bye bye. Abu Muhammad, greetings, greetings, greetings.

802
00:47:26,000 --> 00:47:27,000
Silavê me ji wekî gora hene.
 
Our greetings are with the likes of you [the viewers].

803
00:47:27,000 --> 00:47:47,000
Arê, bay bay.
 
Yes, bye bye.

804
00:48:01,000 --> 00:48:05,000
Arê, hevalno, li vî derê me vîdya xwe xîtam kiribû.
 
Yes, friends, we had ended our video at this place.

805
00:48:05,000 --> 00:48:08,000
Tabeen, Ebû Salah...
 
Naturally, Abu Salah...

806
00:48:08,000 --> 00:48:12,000
Evna tirba miriyê gund e. Xwedê rehma xwe lêke cîyê xwe
cinet be.
 
This is the grave of the village dead. May God have mercy on
him, may his place be paradise.

807
00:48:12,000 --> 00:48:15,000
E welle xeberek nexweş jî me... me ro wago.
 
And by God, an unpleasant news we... we said today.

808
00:48:15,000 --> 00:48:19,000
Hev lawkî gund e, Xwedê rehma xwe lêke. Çend salî bû xolû?
 
This is a young man of the village, may God have mercy on
him. How old was he uncle?

809
00:48:19,000 --> 00:48:20,000
Dav-hevd.
 
Seven-teen.

810
00:48:20,000 --> 00:48:21,000
Dav-hevd salî bû.
 
He was seventeen years old.

811
00:48:21,000 --> 00:48:25,000
Çûbû ber avê Gemrûkê, xolû dibê ket avê, ber şelal.
 
He had gone near the Gamrouk water, uncle says he fell in
the water, near the waterfall.

812
00:48:25,000 --> 00:48:27,000
Dibê em çel pênc merê li wir bûn.
 
He says we were forty-five men there.

813
00:48:27,000 --> 00:48:31,000
E li wî derê dibê, tewar bî, ma nekarbûnî derxistbûya.
 
And there he says, it happened, we couldn't get him out.

814
00:48:31,000 --> 00:48:36,000
Dibê canê can, li pişî makê bifase û nû kes nukanî derxe.
 
He says life is life, [he got stuck] behind a rock and no
one could get him out.

815
00:48:36,000 --> 00:48:38,000
Kişandî bû bin vê ber qafê.
 
It had pulled him under this rocky ledge.

816
00:48:38,000 --> 00:48:40,000
E dworda, wekî dibê...
 
And there, as he says...

817
00:48:40,000 --> 00:48:43,000
Rehmetî bî, Xwedê rehma xwe lêke, cîyê xwe cinet be.
 
He passed away, may God have mercy on him, may his place be
paradise.

818
00:48:43,000 --> 00:48:44,000
Çend sal na rehmetî biye?
 
How many years since he passed away?

819
00:48:44,000 --> 00:48:45,000
Du sal.
 
Two years.

820
00:48:45,000 --> 00:48:47,000
Du sal na rehmetî biye, xolû dibê du sal na rehmetî biye.
 
Two years since he passed away, uncle says it's been two
years since he passed away.

821
00:48:47,000 --> 00:48:49,000
Xwedê rehma xwe lêke, cîyê xwe cinet be.
 
May God have mercy on him, may his place be paradise.

822
00:48:49,000 --> 00:48:55,000
Ev mriyê xwa ne.
 
This is their deceased.

823
00:48:55,000 --> 00:49:09,000
[Music starts]
 
[Music starts]

824
00:49:09,000 --> 00:49:12,000
Ebû Mhemed.
 
Abu Muhammad.

825
00:49:12,000 --> 00:49:15,000
Av zûrê te ra dikişim.
 
I am taking this zoom for you.

826
00:49:15,000 --> 00:49:17,000
Ooo, gaf rom.
 
Ooo, [Gaf Rom - likely referring to a steep/difficult road
or local landmark].

827
00:49:17,000 --> 00:49:27,000
Ebû Mhemed.
 
Abu Muhammad.

828
00:49:27,000 --> 00:49:32,000
Berbî hewşa gever da bî. Cûz em di jor a harin, poşx we
hewşa bo me bikşîne, erê.
 
It was towards the upper courtyard. Since we are going up,
film that courtyard for us, yes.

829
00:49:32,000 --> 00:49:43,000
O vê jî bigir.
 
Film this one too.

830
00:49:43,000 --> 00:49:45,000
Gund xeyiriye ne, Ebû Mhemed gund xeyiriye ne?
 
The village has changed right, Abu Muhammad the village has
changed right?

831
00:49:45,000 --> 00:49:52,000
Tabeen gund ke bigeyre.
 
Naturally, the village changes.

832
00:49:52,000 --> 00:50:12,000
Voda mal tune ne.
 
There are no houses over here.

833
00:50:54,000 --> 00:50:57,000
Ya rebî mala we ava, ka dernaka işim pê tê ne.
 
Oh Lord, may your home be prosperous, let's see if my work
comes out right.

834
00:50:57,000 --> 00:51:02,000
Heta tiliyê me heta qûnê me, ez ketime baskê hewşo vî
darxim.
 
From my fingers to my backside, I have fallen into the
corner of the courtyard to weave this.

835
00:51:02,000 --> 00:51:07,000
Bes wele kin, wele ez vî sibe da derketime, wo dênê ke êvar
bibê.
 
Just look, by God I have been out since this morning, and
look, it has become evening.

836
00:51:07,000 --> 00:51:09,000
Yanî menî û lûmo ji min nekin.
 
So don't make excuses or blame me.

837
00:51:09,000 --> 00:51:13,000
Gemer, qûk nemaye heta molqînê, dênê ke şev reş bûye.
 
Filth, no clean spot has remained up to the neck, look the
night has become black.

838
00:51:13,000 --> 00:51:15,000
Yanî yek wek sibe de derketiyê heta nîv şev.
 
Meaning one who has gone out from morning until midnight.

839
00:51:15,000 --> 00:51:18,000
Û yek mal jî hene di paş şev da ne, xuy natin.
 
And there is a family [waiting] late in the night, sleep
doesn't come [to them].

840
00:51:18,000 --> 00:51:38,000
Yanî hunê qisûrê efû kin. Pir pir.
 
Meaning you will forgive the fault. Very much.

841
00:51:56,000 --> 00:51:59,000
Kuro Mihemed, ew emmê te Gindî wane zeytûna...
 
Son Mohammed, is that your Uncle Gindi and them [at] the
olives...

842
00:51:59,000 --> 00:52:04,000
Ha we li marê xwarê kan?
 
Where are the houses down there?

